  "design_notes": [
    "Two statistically independent groups (different baselines and different outlier sets): the HSTree window, SHAP background and worker of each group are independent.",
    "Exactly one cross-group timestamp collision (both event 100) proves that the (Group, source_event_id) key never mixes the groups, unlike the OC-12 single-group key.",
    "OC-12-proven shape: baseline vectors identical inside each group, unseen outliers far away, HSTREE_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE=100 -> events 1..99 warmup, events 100..101 computed with a still-null hstree_anomaly (threshold_warmup), events 102..110 strictly boolean verdicts.",
    "SHAP_NSAMPLES stays at the production value 100; EXPLAINABILITY_SEED is the only varied setting across runs (reference 42, secondary 43 and 44).",
    "Alpha and Beta use DIFFERENT baselines: any cross-group contamination would break the reproducibility or the expected verdicts.",
    "additivity_tolerance is DEDICATED and deliberately looser than numeric_tolerances: the KernelSHAP identity base + sum(shap_values) ~= local_hstree_score goes through an ill-conditioned weighted regression, so it is not expected to hold bit-for-bit. The strict 1e-12 tolerances stay reserved for same-seed reproducibility between two runs."
  ],
